  {
    title: "Replace hardcoded sample quotes in EvidenceStream with an honest empty state",
    description: "EvidenceStream renders hardcoded Gong/Slack quotes (JOB-402, O-1, O-2) that look like ingested calls. A small note says nothing is wired up, but the figures still masquerade as real evidence — misleading users.",
    acceptance: "Empty state shows a neutral icon + one-sentence explanation; a CTA button opens Settings → Connectors; no sample figures rendered.",
    files: "components/canvas/EvidenceStream.tsx (lines 1-29)",
    prompt: "Replace the hardcoded <figure> blocks with an empty-state render guarded on whether any evidence exists for the active job. Add an onClick that calls openSettings() from useStudio() when the CTA is pressed. Keep new markup in the component's CSS module if it owns one. Add/extend EvidenceStream.test.tsx to assert the empty state renders when no evidence exists and that no .evidence-figure is present. Run `npm --prefix apps/studio run lint && npm --prefix apps/studio run typecheck && npm --prefix apps/studio test -- --run` and ensure green before handoff.",
    effort: "~1h",
  },
  {
    title: "Remove fake connector status rows from SettingsPanel",
    description: "SettingsPanel renders three hardcoded `<li>` rows (Gong transcripts, Slack friction stream, Product telemetry) always as `not connected` with no way to connect them — a dead-end.",
    acceptance: "Three rows removed; honest message plus pointer to Presets dropdown.",
    files: "components/SettingsPanel.tsx (lines 134-148)",
    prompt: "Delete the three <li> rows and replace with a single static message element. Render a pointer that opens the Presets catalog area. Add an assertion in SettingsPanel.test.tsx that the fake hostnames no longer appear. Run lint/typecheck/test before handoff.",
    effort: "~30m",
  },
